      "writtenOn": "2026-10-08T23:46:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Jetski claims this - \n\n-------------\n\n1. No conflict on .git-blame-ignore-revs: AutoMerger writes the merged tree (either to refs/cache-automerge/ or in-memory via InMemoryInserter). Because GetBlame.apply initializes revWalk over ins.newReader(), IgnoreRevFileReader.read(revWalk, id) reads the automerge tree and .git-blame-ignore-revs blob in both cases. Added withIgnoreRevsFileInMergeCommit in GetBlameIT (PS2) to cover forBase(true) on a 2-parent merge commit.\n\n2. Content conflict on .git-blame-ignore-revs: AutoMerger calls MergeUtil.mergeWithConflicts, which writes the conflicted file as a normal stage-0 blob in the automerge tree with standard \u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c / \u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d / \u003e\u003e\u003e\u003e\u003e\u003e\u003e conflict markers. IgnoreRevFileReader skips the non-hex conflict marker lines and still parses all valid 40-char SHAs from both parents (and for a modify/delete conflict, MergeUtil keeps the existing stage entry).\n\n-------------",
      "parentUuid": "fa517857_0ea3be77",
      "revId": "6db1368e5d70cb0213a85a10ce19be30744eff2c",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
